[48.997275, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Session: session-20261113-152234-644-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Permissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Tip: Run \u001b[1mami --skill <name>\u001b[22m to pin a skill stance for the session.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Activate the cognitive-doc-design skill, then use its guidance to write a README.md here for a \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255msmall CLI tool called 'tinycount' (a word/line/char counter for files). Keep it concise and \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mwell-structured. When finished, print the final README.md to the terminal. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll activate the cognitive-doc-design skill and use its guidance to create a clean, well-structured\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KREADME for tinycount.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;208m\u25b6 \u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;35m\u25cf \u001b[39m\u001b[2mRan skill(Skill \"cognitive-doc-design\" activated inline. ...) 0.0s\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KNow I'll create a well-structured README for tinycount using the cognitive-doc-design principles.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll focus on leading with the answer, progressive disclosure, and clear signposting.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m[Checkpoint cp-1794579803184-1: /tmp/ami-demo-K5y26U/README.md]\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;167m\u25cf\u001b[39m \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;167mfile_edit\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;243m/tmp/ami-demo-K5y26U/README.md\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[39mfile_edit /tmp/ami-demo-K5y26U/README.